# Build-time public configuration for the web app.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* belongs here — everything in this file is compiled into
# the client bundle and is world-readable. Never put a secret here.
#
# NODE_ENV is deliberately absent: `next build` sets it to production itself,
# and injecting NODE_ENV=development from the shared .env silently broke the
# build for weeks with a misleading "<Html> should not be imported" error.
#
# Left EMPTY on purpose. The deployment sets these as build-time environment
# variables in Vercel, pointing at the API's own domain. A localhost value
# here would be compiled into the public bundle — which is exactly why the
# first deployment called the visitor's own machine.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
